A turn that starts its next request as its core looks at it again leaves the timer as it was set.
The timer would let the new request's end pass, and a thread without spare time run on past what its units paid for;
a request's end is the timer's to mark.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets the end of the turn's request pass
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-goes-renews

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1356,8 +1356,6 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) bool deadline_due(struct core *core)
             return core->run_queue != 0;
         }
         request_renew(own, p, now);
-        /* Its end is the timer's to mark. */
-        core->wake_stale = true;
     }
     return core->run_queue != 0 && due_before(run_earliest(core)->deadline, own->deadline);
 }
